data: {"step": "response", "status": "streaming", "detail": "No, not identically. The two FIRs related to the online banking fraud matter\u2014**FIR 64/26** and **FIR 65/26**\u2014were not processed and recorded the same way.  \n\n- **FIR 64/26** has a matching walk-in complaint recorded in the CMS system (case tag **CMS-ISB-2026-0341**) [Document 3].  \n- **FIR 65/26** does not appear in the CMS linkage list, indicating no corresponding walk-in complaint was recorded for this case [Document 3].  \n\nBoth FIRs are registered under the **PECA 2016** statute and involve accused individuals (e.g., **\u0639\u0627\u0635\u0645 \u0631\u0634\u06cc\u062f** appears in both) [Document 2], but the presence of a linked CMS complaint for **FIR 64/26** and its absence for **FIR 65/26** reflects a difference in how the cases were documented in the complaint management system.\n\n_A cited claim ([Document 2]) could only be partially confirmed against its source: The source confirms \u0639\u0627\u0635\u0645 \u0631\u0634\u06cc\u062f appears in both FIRs but does not mention PECA 2016 or the comparison of documentation practices._"}

